    {
      "id": "notes",
      "title": "Notes",
      "groups": [
        {
          "style": {
            "widthInches": 10,
            "wrap": true
          },
          "detail": [
            {
              "title": "Notes applicable to the All Schools, Maintained Schools, Academies and NMSS tabs",
              "style": {
                "bold": true
              }
            },
            {
              "title": "1. Eligible Year 1 and Year 2 pupil counts include National Curriculum not followed pupils, aged 4, 5 and 6.",
              "classname": "borderAllSides",
              "style": {
                "wrap": true
              }
            },
            {
              "title": "2. The provisional revenue payment for 2022-23 is the total number of eligible meals taken in 2021-22 multiplied by the 2022-23 daily meal rate by 190 days and by 7/12ths.",
              "classname": "borderAllSides",
              "style": {
                "wrap": true
              }
            },
            {
              "title": "3. The total eligible meals taken by Reception pupils used in the 2021-22 final allocation calculation is the higher of, the average number of eligible meals taken by Reception pupils across the October 2021 and January 2022 censuses, or the number of eligible meals taken by Reception pupils in the January 2022 census. Pupils are only counted when in eligible school types.",
              "classname": "borderAllSides",
              "style": {
                "wrap": true
              }
            },
            {
              "title": "4. The total eligible meals taken by Year 1 and Year 2 pupils used in the 2021-22 final allocation calculation is the average number of eligible meals taken by Year 1 and Year 2 pupils across the October 20221 and January 2022 censuses. Pupils are only counted when in eligible school types.",
              "classname": "borderAllSides",
              "style": {
                "wrap": true
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
